``

New:
```js
function parseSleepMilliseconds(ms) {
  return Math.max(0, parseInt(ms, 10) || 0);
}

function hasJavaThread() {
  return typeof Java !== 'undefined' && Java.type;
}

function sleepViaJavaThread(ms) {
  Java.type('java.lang.Thread').sleep(ms);
}

function sleepViaBusyWait(ms) {
  var end = Date.now() + ms;
  while (Date.now() < end) {}

// Pauses the current thread for the given duration. Trivial on purpose: the
// duration parsing and the engine-specific sleep strategies live in the small
// helpers above, so this reads as a decision table and stays injectable.
function sleepMilliseconds(ms) {
  var duration = parseSleepMilliseconds(ms);
  if (duration <= 0) return;
  if (hasJavaThread()) {
      sleepViaJavaThread(duration);
      return;
  }
  sleepViaBusyWait(duration);
}
``

CC check:
- parseSleepMilliseconds: 1 + 1(||) = 2
- hasJavaThread: 1 + 1(&) = 2
- sleepViaJavaThread: 1
- sleepViaBusyWait: 1 + 1(while) = 2
- sleepMilliseconds: 1 + 1 + 1 = 3

Coverage in node harness: parse (all via direct tests), hasJavaThread both branches (with/without Java mock), javaThreadSleep (Java mock test), busyWait (plain test), sleepMilliseconds: all paths. All fully covered → CRAP = CC.

